        "problem": "Find the solution to the inequality $1<\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$\\,x\\le $\n\n{{field-3}}",
        "worked_solution": "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\nFirst, we multiply by $3$ to eliminate the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & <\\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot 1 & <3\\cdot \\frac{x+5}{3}\\le 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3 & <x+5\\le 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we continue isolating $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & <x+5\\le 6 \\\\ 3-5 & <x+5-5\\le 6-5 \\\\ -2 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $-2<x\\le 1.$",
